<%#
  Every .kicad_sch/.kicad_pcb anywhere in the folder, plus ONE inline KiCanvas preview — the
  private partial's shape (projects/_schematics.html.erb) with public URLs.

  THE PREVIEW URL IS THE NAMED FORM, EXTENSION LAST, AND THE TOKEN RIDES ALONG. KiCanvas reads a
  file's type off the URL it fetches, not off the bytes, so the route's optional `*filename` glob
  carries the real name — which is also why that route is declared `format: false` (a trailing
  `.kicad_sch` must not be parsed as a response format).

  THE LIST LINKS ARE `download: true` ON PURPOSE. A .kicad_sch is not an inline-safe type, so the
  concern would attach it anyway; saying so in the URL means the link and the button a visitor
  reaches for agree. Since stage 4, S4-5 a visitor DOES have a file page to be sent to
  (`/u/:handle/:slug/files/:id/view`, which mounts KiCanvas for any schematic, not only the first);
  this list still links the bytes by decision — it is the download list, the page above it is the
  viewer, and the file page is one click from the project page's Files list.

  Local: pub (Maker::PublicProject).
%>
<% if pub.kicad_rows.any? %>
  <section class="panel schematics-panel">
    <h2>Schematics</h2>
    <ul class="schematics-list">
      <% pub.kicad_rows.each do |row| %>
        <% ext = File.extname(row.node.name).downcase.delete(".") %>
        <li>
          <%= link_to row.node.name, pub.file_url_for(row.node_id, download: true) %>
          <span class="badge"><%= ext == "kicad_sch" ? "schematic" : "board" %></span>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
    <% preview = pub.kicad_rows.first %>
    <div class="kicanvas-stage schematics-preview"
         data-controller="kicanvas"
         data-kicanvas-url-value="<%= pub.file_url_for(preview.node_id, filename: preview.node.name) %>"
         data-kicanvas-controls-value="basic">
      <p class="muted" data-kicanvas-target="status">Loading the viewer…</p>
      <div data-kicanvas-target="stage"></div>
    </div>
  </section>
<% end %>
